7bc2074eb6283dcff21f4d8dc1ac28d43f33","position":"1794472351098036001-ecf73943-0fcf-4127-a62b-d99230873d52"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"ca58207d426712eed2d763b9f77ee6826d0c572a21024c8b1b715aaa99e8b5d9","event_uuid":"f0b09313-e45f-4d20-8972-f710d7634e91","position":{"commit_sha":"70d560098e54d450e225cb04764c75b1c7efe3dd","position":"1794472400516928427-f0b09313-e45f-4d20-8972-f710d7634e91"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify evidence (AC4): `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` in worktree engine-switch at commit 6216427b41e (the tree pushed as Gerrit 3362 patch set 1), 2026-11-11 22:30-23:51 PST, exit code 0. Lint \"All checks passed!\"; import-convention \"3 passed\"; default tier \"21136 passed, 29 skipped, 19 warnings in 4330.32s\"; integration tier \"218 passed, 2 skipped in 335.59s\". Gerrit 3362: LLM-Review +1 (1 advisory: the refresh test asserts the intermediate fields dict rather than the built manifest), Verified +1 (Actions run 43178565004), 0 unresolved; merged as 940d80765bd18f8c95defa3cf4389c820f16a94a at 2026-11-12 00:23 PST.\nAC1-AC3 are pinned by tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py (9 tests): agentic PASS signs `engine: agentic`, status certified/agentic, claim and close_plan_review_gate_check accept; sign-review keeps the line; refresh carries the prior engine; pipeline manifests are byte-identical and read pipeline; unknown values read pipeline; the plaintext manifest copy is non-authoritative and rewriting the signed payload breaks verification; agentic BLOCK and INDETERMINATE write no attestation (status engine null, schema-valid).","timestamp":1794471885092117929},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 00:33 PST: CLOSED through the completion-verifier gate at 00:32 PST. Gerrit 3362 merged as 940d80765bd. The plan took 3 review rounds (r1 BLOCK: missed status key-set pin; r2 PASS, then scope widened to tests/unit/test_output_schemas.py (the narrow-schema pin), r3 PASS). The 1 LLM-Review advisory (refresh test asserts the intermediate fields, not the built manifest) is minor and recorded here, not filed. Unblocked: churlish-zircon-rhea (surfaces), now under review.","timestamp":1794472400516928427}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794255906559413001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"49529de1-03a4-4a3e-9053-9bb22c796c7f","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"75af-1212-aa22-463f"},{"link_uuid":"7c3021a5-9693-4034-9200-84495eb68b44","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7aff-f40a-f35a-44e0"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA non-blocking PASS under either engine earns the same certification: a signed plan-review attestation that the claim gate, close gate, `review-plan --status` and `sign-review` accept (ADR 0049). Since [rebar:confident-snooty-stinkpot], an agentic PASS is signed through the same `_finalize_signature` → `attest.sign_plan_review` path, and every agentic verdict carries `coverage.engine = \"agentic\"`; pipeline verdicts carry no `engine` key. The signed manifest does not record which engine produced it, so the two engines cannot be audited side by side once sidecars are pruned (`sidecar.prune`, 50 per ticket).\n\n## Approach\n\n**Signed field.** `manifest.build_manifest` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:478`) appends `engine: agentic` when the verdict's `coverage.engine` is `\"agentic\"`, the only non-pipeline engine `plan_review.PLAN_REVIEW_ENGINES` defines; any other value writes nothing. A pipeline manifest is byte-identical to today's, so no existing or future pipeline attestation changes. The line is inside the signed bytes (the signature binds `(ticket_id, manifest)`), so editing it breaks verification. Manifest readers already ignore unknown lines (`manifest.py:14`), so claim, close, `--status` and `sign-review` accept the new line unchanged. New reader `manifest_engine(manifest) -> str` returns the line's value when it is a known engine, else `\"pipeline\"`, so every attestation signed before this change reads as pipeline. ADR 0123 §5's `engine` field is thus always readable while pipeline manifests stay byte-identical. No migration. Agentic attestations signed between [rebar:confident-snooty-stinkpot] and this change also read as pipeline. None exist in the shared store: the agentic engine has run only in tests, and the production MCP workspace predates it. `sign-review` restores the line from the sidecar for any that do.\n\n**Carried through every re-sign.**\n- `sign-review` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py`) rebuilds the verdict from the stored sidecar, including its `coverage` (`resign.py:337`), and calls `build_manifest`. The agentic sidecar's `coverage.engine` therefore reaches the re-signed manifest with no resign change. A test pins it.\n- `attest.refresh_attestation` (drift refresh) rebuilds the verdict from the prior manifest's fields. It gains `fields[\"coverage\"][\"engine\"] = manifest_engine(prior_manifest)`. A refresh re-binds the PRIOR verdict to current hashes after a cheap probe and never re-reviews, so the engine that produced that verdict is still the right provenance. `manifest_engine` lives in `manifest.py` (709 lines) and, per that module's rule, is re-exported from `attest` (import block and `__all__`). `attest.py` (786 lines) grows by about 3 lines.\n\n**Surfaced.** `attest_gate.plan_review_status` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py:202`) adds `engine`: the signed attestation's `manifest_engine`, or `None` when no readable certified attestation exists, beside `currency_basis`. This one function backs the CLI `review-plan --status` JSON and the MCP `plan_review_status` tool. `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json` gains the optional `engine` property (`\"pipeline\"`, `\"agentic\"` or null). It stays out of `required`, so older readers are unaffected. `docs/plan-review-gate.md` documents the field.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py (`engine:` line, `manifest_engine`)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py (refresh carries engine)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py (status field)\n- src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json\n- docs/plan-review-gate.md\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py (new)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_discovery.py (`test_review_plan_status_stays_narrow` key set gains `engine`)\n- tests/unit/test_output_schemas.py (the pinned narrow `PLAN_REVIEW_STATUS` property set gains `engine`, the deliberate reviewable growth that pin asks for)\n\n## Testing\n\nAll tests run offline with a counting FakeRunner and real signing in a temp repo.\n\n- Happy path: an agentic PASS signs a manifest containing `engine: agentic`. `plan_review_status` reports `certified` with `engine == \"agentic\"`, `claim` succeeds, and `_commands.gates.close_plan_review_gate_check` accepts the attestation.\n- Unknown value: a verdict with `coverage.engine == \"other\"` writes no line, and a manifest line `engine: other` reads as `\"pipeline\"`.\n- Re-sign: after the reviewed code drifts, `sign-review` re-certifies the agentic attestation, and the new manifest still carries `engine: agentic`. `refresh_attestation` on an agentic prior manifest also keeps it.\n- Back-compat: a pipeline PASS manifest has no `engine:` line, is byte-identical to the manifest built without the change, and reads as `\"pipeline\"`. `plan_review_status` reports `engine == \"pipeline\"`.\n- Tamper: rewriting `engine: agentic` to `engine: pipeline` in a signed record fails `signing.verify_signature`.\n- Refusal: an agentic BLOCK and an agentic INDETERMINATE write no attestation, and `engine` is `None` on status.\n- `plan_review_status` output validates against `plan_review_status.schema.json` both with `engine` set and with it null.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Agentic PASS attestations record `engine: agentic` inside the signed manifest. Claim, close, `review-plan --status`, `sign-review` and drift refresh accept and preserve it, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py`.\n- [x] Pipeline manifests are byte-identical, and pre-existing attestations without the line read as `\"pipeline\"`, pinned by the back-compat test.\n- [x] Tampering with the field fails signature verification, pinned by the tamper test.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py","reason":"engine line, manifest_engine"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","reason":"refresh carries engine, re-export"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py","reason":"status engine field"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json","reason":"engine property"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"document field"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py","reason":"new tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_discovery.py","reason":"status key set"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_output_schemas.py","reason":"narrow schema pin"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["depends_on","75af-1212-aa22-463f"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","7aff-f40a-f35a-44e0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"70596971-b4aa-431b-ac7a-77b37272ec0f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4cc4-3b8b-e554-41ef","ticket_type":"story","title":"Record the plan-review engine on the signed attestation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a3452c2d-dd43-43d6-8088-f786e38f5967","f3507ded-6319-42bb-ab90-a935da20852b","69553bc4-fdef-4753-8509-7247c0affcca","280674db-e477-423d-b445-fe83c955a55d","678f7509-4adc-4c41-a3f1-3f66c90ca6b3","e21742d6-bcf4-40fa-9f38-5cc7470e741e","0222cbfc-3aac-452c-a0f7-18fe9815e350","07cd192a-0283-4e5c-b89f-d54d4aa2bc65","e0664bbe-c8bd-40e7-a740-2f6eb969a1ed","2d3cf893-a0eb-4ed1-8fac-4546d56fcfe1","7c3021a5-9693-4034-9200-84495eb68b44","e534b274-ed8b-4844-8fa0-87f24e8d83cb","f50a9cb1-eb18-42b6-8d13-02ee0b8cec7d","70596971-b4aa-431b-ac7a-77b37272ec0f","ecf73943-0fcf-4127-a62b-d99230873d52","f0b09313-e45f-4d20-8972-f710d7634e91"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794472400516928428,"uuid":"b69f669f-473e-4530-a98c-d34fe8abe514"}